## Description

The `tryCompressChat` function in `packages/core/src/core/client.ts` attempts to
compress the chat history if it exceeds a certain token threshold.

In certain scenarios, such as when the history contains only a single, large
context message, the `findCompressSplitPoint` function returns 0. This results
in `historyToCompress` being an empty array.

The code then proceeds to make an API call to the model to summarize this empty
`historyToCompress`. This is an unnecessary API call that wastes resources, adds
latency, and could potentially result in an error from the API.

## Location

`packages/core/src/core/client.ts` within the `tryCompressChat` method.

## Proposed Solution

Add a check after `historyToCompress` is calculated. If it is empty, return a
`NOOP` status immediately to avoid the unnecessary API call.

```typescript
// packages/core/src/core/client.ts

// ... after findCompressSplitPoint

const historyToCompress = curatedHistory.slice(0, splitPoint);
const historyToKeep = curatedHistory.slice(splitPoint);

// Add this check
if (historyToCompress.length === 0) {
  return {
    originalTokenCount,
    newTokenCount: originalTokenCount,
    compressionStatus: CompressionStatus.NOOP,
  };
}

const summaryResponse = await this.config;
// ...
```

This change ensures that compression is only attempted when there is actual conversation history to compress beyond the initial context.
